From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jared Baur <jaredbaur@fastmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 01:36:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] importer: open bytecode caches read-only

`get_data` only ever reads: it is called with the `.lpyc` cache path from
`_exec_cached_module`, and with the `.lpy` source path by the inherited
`SourceLoader.get_source`. Opening those in `r+b` needlessly demands write
permission, so on a read-only install prefix every one of those reads raises
`OSError`.

For the cache path that error is caught and treated as a cache miss, sending
every import down the recompile path and then failing in `set_data`. For the
source path it breaks `inspect.getsource`, `linecache` traceback context and
pydoc on any installed namespace.

Open for reading only, which is all the method does.
---
 src/basilisp/importer.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/basilisp/importer.py b/src/basilisp/importer.py
index 5796f4f..313fbdb 100644
--- a/src/basilisp/importer.py
+++ b/src/basilisp/importer.py
@@ -215,7 +215,7 @@ class BasilispImporter(  # type: ignore[misc]  # pylint: disable=abstract-method
         return {"mtime": int(stat.st_mtime), "size": stat.st_size}
 
     def get_data(self, path: str) -> bytes:
-        with open(path, mode="r+b") as f:
+        with open(path, mode="rb") as f:
             return f.read()
 
     def set_data(self, path: str, data: bytes) -> None:
